{
  "description": "Every path no grant may reach, for every backend. ONE cross-platform list, unlike the two operating-system grant files beside it: both platform spellings are present on every host, because a config authored on one platform can be applied on another, and `the_shared_floor_covers_what_each_backend_refused_separately` asserts both groups ungated. `rule` is the security decision on every row: `exact` refuses a grant naming this path and leaves a path inside it grantable, `overlap` refuses a grant at it, under it, or above it. `class` says what the row protects, which decides its message and whether `allow_credential_store` may exempt it — only `credential_store` may. `permits` names the cells the row lets through, because a workload may stat what it cannot read; a permit names a cell, never a path.",
